{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And I.</b> We know that the Sea of Reeds is not between Egypt and the land of Israel, and there was no need for them to enter the sea. Only HaShem commanded to do so so that the Egyptians would enter after them and drown. And from the wilderness of Etham Israel entered into the sea, and to the wilderness of Etham they came out, as I shall explain:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:25.458387392Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}